message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "SC Sim Framework: a transferable and composable simulation framework for supply chain digital twins"
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-20
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/beateruel/sc_sim_framework"
authors:
  - family-names: Royo
    given-names: Beatriz
    affiliation: "Fundación Zaragoza Logistics Center (ZLC)"
  - family-names: de la Cruz
    given-names: María Teresa
    affiliation: "Fundación Zaragoza Logistics Center (ZLC)"
abstract: "Open-source Python implementation of a methodology that translates SCOR process representations into executable supply chain simulation models. It includes a time-stepped Make-to-Stock plastic injection model and a SimPy discrete-event Make-to-Order apparel model, with configuration files, scenario experiments and stochastic robustness tests."
keywords:
  - supply chain digital twin
  - SCOR
  - BPMN
  - simulation
  - make-to-stock
  - make-to-order